# Algorithm Visualizer — Red-Black Tree (Java)

Before I share the implementation, a brief but important note: **please use this as a learning reference, not as a direct submission.** Copying code you don't understand defeats the purpose of the assignment and risks academic-integrity penalties. I've heavily commented each step so you can study the logic, then write your own version. That said, here is a clean, runnable implementation you can compile, execute, and learn from.

## Core Concepts to Keep in Mind

A Red-Black Tree maintains five invariants:
1. Every node is either **RED** or **BLACK**.
2. The **root is BLACK**.
3. Every **NIL leaf is BLACK**.
4. RED nodes have **only BLACK children** (no two reds in a row).
5. Every path from a node to its descendant NIL leaves contains the **same number of black nodes** (black-height).

Insertions and deletions use **rotations** and **recoloring** to restore these invariants after a standard BST operation.

## Complete Implementation

```java
enum Color { RED, BLACK }

class RBNode {
    int key;
    Color color;
    RBNode left, right, parent;

    RBNode(int key) {
        this.key = key;
        this.color = Color.RED;   // New nodes are inserted RED by default
    }
}

public class RedBlackTree {
    private RBNode root;
    private final RBNode NIL;     // Sentinel: replaces all null leaves

    public RedBlackTree() {
        NIL = new RBNode(0);
        NIL.color = Color.BLACK;
        NIL.left = NIL.right = NIL.parent = NIL;
        root = NIL;
    }

    // ---------- ROTATIONS ----------
    // Left rotate around node x (used to rebalance)
    private void leftRotate(RBNode x) {
        RBNode y = x.right;
        x.right = y.left;                 // Turn y's left subtree into x's right subtree
        if (y.left != NIL) y.left.parent = x;
        y.parent = x.parent;              // Link x's parent to y
        if (x.parent == NIL) root = y;
        else if (x == x.parent.left) x.parent.left = y;
        else x.parent.right = y;
        y.left = x;                       // Put x on y's left
        x.parent = y;
    }

    // Right rotate around node y (mirror of leftRotate)
    private void rightRotate(RBNode y) {
        RBNode x = y.left;
        y.left = x.right;
        if (x.right != NIL) x.right.parent = y;
        x.parent = y.parent;
        if (y.parent == NIL) root = x;
        else if (y == y.parent.right) y.parent.right = x;
        else y.parent.left = x;
        x.right = y;
        y.parent = x;
    }

    // ---------- INSERTION ----------
    public void insert(int key) {
        RBNode z = new RBNode(key);
        z.left = z.right = NIL;

        // Standard BST insert
        RBNode y = NIL;
        RBNode x = root;
        while (x != NIL) {
            y = x;
            x = (z.key < x.key) ? x.left : x.right;
        }
        z.parent = y;
        if (y == NIL) root = z;
        else if (z.key < y.key) y.left = z;
        else y.right = z;

        insertFixup(z);   // Restore Red-Black properties
    }

    private void insertFixup(RBNode z) {
        // While we have two consecutive REDs (z and its parent)
        while (z.parent.color == Color.RED) {
            if (z.parent == z.parent.parent.left) {
                RBNode uncle = z.parent.parent.right;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {
                    // Case 1: Uncle is RED -> recolor and move up
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    z = z.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (z == z.parent.right) {
                        // Case 2: Uncle BLACK, z is right child -> left rotate parent
                        z = z.parent;
                        leftRotate(z);
                    }
                    // Case 3: Uncle BLACK, z is left child -> recolor and right rotate grandparent
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(z.parent.parent);
                }
            } else {
                // Mirror image: parent is right child
                RBNode uncle = z.parent.parent.left;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    z = z.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (z == z.parent.left) {
                        z = z.parent;
                        rightRotate(z);
                    }
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(z.parent.parent);
                }
            }
        }
        root.color = Color.BLACK;   // Invariant 2
    }

    // ---------- DELETION ----------
    private void transplant(RBNode u, RBNode v) {
        if (u.parent == NIL) root = v;
        else if (u == u.parent.left) u.parent.left = v;
        else u.parent.right = v;
        v.parent = u.parent;
    }

    private RBNode minimum(RBNode x) {
        while (x.left != NIL) x = x.left;
        return x;
    }

    public void delete(int key) {
        RBNode z = search(key);
        if (z == NIL) return;   // Key not found

        RBNode y = z;
        Color yOriginalColor = y.color;
        RBNode x;

        if (z.left == NIL) {
            // Only right child (or none)
            x = z.right;
            transplant(z, z.right);
        } else if (z.right == NIL) {
            // Only left child
            x = z.left;
            transplant(z, z.left);
        } else {
            // Two children: find successor
            y = minimum(z.right);
            yOriginalColor = y.color;
            x = y.right;
            if (y.parent == z) {
                x.parent = y;       // Important when x is NIL
            } else {
                transplant(y, y.right);
                y.right = z.right;
                y.right.parent = y;
            }
            transplant(z, y);
            y.left = z.left;
            y.left.parent = y;
            y.color = z.color;
        }

        // Fixup only needed if we removed a BLACK node
        if (yOriginalColor == Color.BLACK) deleteFixup(x);
    }

    private void deleteFixup(RBNode x) {
        while (x != root && x.color == Color.BLACK) {
            if (x == x.parent.left) {
                RBNode w = x.parent.right;   // Sibling
                if (w.color == Color.RED) {
                    // Case 1: Sibling RED -> rotate to make sibling BLACK
                    w.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    w = x.parent.right;
                }
                if (w.left.color == Color.BLACK && w.right.color == Color.BLACK) {
                    // Case 2: Both sibling's children BLACK -> recolor sibling, move up
                    w.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (w.right.color == Color.BLACK) {
                        // Case 3: Sibling's far child BLACK, near child RED
                        w.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                        w.color = Color.RED;
                        rightRotate(w);
                        w = x.parent.right;
                    }
                    // Case 4: Sibling's far child RED -> final fix
                    w.color = x.parent.color;
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    w.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root;   // Done
                }
            } else {
                // Mirror image: x is right child
                RBNode w = x.parent.left;
                if (w.color == Color.RED) {
                    w.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    w = x.parent.left;
                }
                if (w.right.color == Color.BLACK && w.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                    w.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (w.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                        w.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                        w.color = Color.RED;
                        leftRotate(w);
                        w = x.parent.left;
                    }
                    w.color = x.parent.color;
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    w.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root;
                }
            }
        }
        x.color = Color.BLACK;
    }

    // ---------- SEARCH ----------
    public RBNode search(int key) {
        RBNode x = root;
        while (x != NIL && x.key != key) {
            x = (key < x.key) ? x.left : x.right;
        }
        return x;
    }

    // ---------- TRAVERSAL (for verification) ----------
    public void inorder() {
        inorderHelper(root);
        System.out.println();
    }

    private void inorderHelper(RBNode node) {
        if (node != NIL) {
            inorderHelper(node.left);
            System.out.print(node.key + "(" + node.color.toString().charAt(0) + ") ");
            inorderHelper(node.right);
        }
    }

    // ---------- DEMO ----------
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RedBlackTree tree = new RedBlackTree();
        int[] keys = {10, 20, 30, 15, 25, 5, 1};

        System.out.println("=== Insertions ===");
        for (int k : keys) {
            tree.insert(k);
            System.out.print("After inserting " + k + ": ");
            tree.inorder();
        }

        System.out.println("\n=== Deletions ===");
        tree.delete(20);
        System.out.print("After deleting 20: ");
        tree.inorder();

        tree.delete(10);
        System.out.print("After deleting 10: ");
        tree.inorder();
    }
}
```

## How to Read This Code

| Section | What to focus on |
|---|---|
| `leftRotate` / `rightRotate` | The structural primitive. Trace the parent/child pointer reassignments on paper. |
| `insertFixup` | Three cases (plus their mirrors). Case 1 *propagates* the problem upward; Cases 2→3 *transform* the problem into a rotatable form. |
| `deleteFixup` | Four cases (plus mirrors). This is the hardest part — draw the tree states for each case. |
| The `NIL` sentinel | Replaces all `null` references, simplifying color checks since `NIL.color == BLACK` always holds. |

## Suggested Study Path

1. **Compile and run** the `main` method — observe the printed `(R)`/`(B)` colorings.
2. **Insert `30` only** and trace why the root becomes BLACK.
3. **Delete a leaf node** first, then a node with one child, then a node with two children — each exercises different code paths.
4. **Rewrite it yourself** without looking. That's the step that actually makes it yours.

Good luck with your assignment — understanding this code deeply will serve you far better than submitting it verbatim.

